cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Deep Hedging Benchmark"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aditya
    family-names: Bhatia
    affiliation: "Stevens Institute of Technology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Adi7710/deep-hedging-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible benchmark for deep hedging. Published deep hedging results are not
  directly comparable, because each paper fixes its own market simulator, transaction
  cost model, convex risk measure, and evaluation metrics. This work defines a single
  frozen protocol and measures, under identical conditions, whether learned hedging
  policies outperform classical transaction-cost bands (Black-Scholes delta,
  Whalley-Wilmott, Zakamouline), and how much of any advantage survives a regime shift
  between training and test distributions.
keywords:
  - deep hedging
  - quantitative finance
  - reproducibility
  - benchmark
  - convex risk measures
  - transaction costs
  - TensorFlow
